{
 "description": "Real DTS-HD Master Audio files from the FFmpeg sample archive: a 7.1 stream of two channel sets (a primary 5.1 set and a set of the rear pair), a 96 kHz 5.0 stream and a 16-bit stereo stream, each a core frame with an extension substream whose first asset has a lossless (XLL) component, cut by the archive (the first two at 5 MiB) or ending inside a frame. The archive allows downloading and states no license for redistribution, so they are downloaded and checked against their SHA-256 rather than committed. Per file: what the analyzer, ffprobe and MediaInfo must report (the first stream of the analyzer's report; the 16-bit file's last, truncated frame starts a second stream of the core alone), the codes of the analyzer's warnings and errors (\"findings\") and of its infos (\"info_findings\"). No real DTS:X or .dtshd file could be found at a public address (the FFmpeg archive has neither), so those are hand-built only.",
